<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Anura Kumara Dissanayake</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. <a href="/years/1968">1968</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Anura Kumara Dissanayake (born 1968) is a Sri Lankan politician who became president of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sri-lanka">Sri Lanka</a> in September 2024. Leader of the left-wing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/janatha-vimukthi-peramuna">Janatha Vimukthi Peramuna</a> from 2014 and of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-peoples-power">National People's Power</a> alliance, he campaigned against corruption after the economic collapse of 2022. His victory was the first for a candidate from outside the established parties, and his alliance won a two-thirds majority in the parliamentary election of November 2024.</p></div>
